Subject: [PATCH 036/155] [ae-patch] Remap every user-id column in the
 accounts-to-OIDC identity migration

remap_identities covered users, grants, comments, policies, account tokens
and hosts. A deployment in use also keys agents, device grants, projects,
scheduled tasks, conversation items, preferences, connections, daily costs
and the turn-actor label on the user id, so after the switch the renamed
user lost their projects, schedules and history attribution. The extra
columns are rewritten in the same transaction, in a new module; user-keyed
rows merge on a forced collision (the new user's preference and connection
win, daily costs add up).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
